  "result": "I found and fixed the bug. `Cart.remove` in `shop/models.py:33` checked each line's display name (`l.item.name`) against the value it was given, but callers pass a SKU. `'sku-1'` never equals `'Widget'`, so the Widget line was never removed. It now checks `l.item.sku`, which is also what `Cart.add` uses to find lines.\n\n**Results:**\n- `python3 -m shop.demo` now prints `1`, meaning only the Gadget is left. Before the fix it would have printed `2`.\n- pytest isn't installed, so I ran the tests with `python3 -m unittest`: all 6 passed.\n\nNo existing test covers `Cart.remove`, so this bug could come back without the tests catching it. I can add one if you'd like.",
